1
00:00:14,056 --> 00:00:15,557
<i>Authorize Hal Jordan.</i>

2
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,352
<i>Access granted.</i>

3
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:21,563
<i>Sinestro.</i>

4
00:00:22,064 --> 00:00:23,272
Hal.

5
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,858
Tell me what you know about Manhunters.

6
00:00:25,692 --> 00:00:28,529
No hello? No how have I been?

7
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:31,990
Hello, Sinestro, how have you been?

8
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:34,826
Now, what the fuck
do you know about Manhunters?

9
00:00:35,369 --> 00:00:36,828
If one still existed,

10
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,874
it'd be the second greatest threat
you're currently facing.

11
00:00:42,626 --> 00:00:44,711
So, why don't you tell me
about John Stewart?

12
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:47,339
Where'd you hear that name?

13
00:00:48,131 --> 00:00:49,132
Around.

14
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:51,218
"Around"?

15
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,637
You're locked up in a cell
in the middle of fucking nowhere.

16
00:00:54,638 --> 00:00:55,973
My trainee has a trainee.

17
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:58,891
It's not unreasonable
for such seismic news

18
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:00,142
to find its way to me.

19
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:01,394
He's not my trainee.

20
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:03,479
He's a contingency plan. A backup.

21
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,855
Where did the Guardians find him?

22
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:07,359
- I don't care where they found him.
- I care, Hal.

23
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:19,454
Marines.

24
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:22,290
They found him in the Marines.

25
00:01:22,291 --> 00:01:25,210
- And that is Earth military.
- What the fuck do you care?

26
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:29,214
You don't really believe
he's your backup, do you, Hal?

27
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:31,883
No.

28
00:01:33,302 --> 00:01:35,220
Then say what he actually is.

29
00:01:41,852 --> 00:01:42,936
My replacement.

30
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:05,374
Hey, Dad.

31
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:06,792
<i>They need to speak with you.</i>

32
00:02:06,793 --> 00:02:08,544
<i>You've got 20 minutes. Get to a pay phone</i>

33
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:09,755
<i>and I'll patch you in.</i>

34
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:13,633
Yeah, I can't right now.

35
00:02:13,634 --> 00:02:15,051
<i>What do you mean you can't?</i>

36
00:02:15,052 --> 00:02:16,594
We're working a case.

37
00:02:16,595 --> 00:02:18,220
Jordan's keeping me busy.

38
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:20,974
<i>Not acceptable.
I'm putting your mother on.</i>

39
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:25,020
<i>Hey, Bernadette,
I got our son on the phone.</i>

40
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:29,566
<i>You really will need
to kill John Stewart, though.</i>

41
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:31,568
<i>No.</i>

42
00:02:32,778 --> 00:02:35,197
- Jordan?
<i>- And why not?</i>

43
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:40,159
Because I'm not evil.

44
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:43,288
No, you're not evil. You're just...

45
00:02:45,999 --> 00:02:47,626
What's that word you're fighting?

46
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:49,669
Old.

47
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,088
Experienced.

48
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:53,964
They want to replace me
with Johnny Try-Hard?

49
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,092
It's fine with me.

50
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,259
The guy's too perfect anyway.

51
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:59,554
Besides that, he's fucking boring.

52
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,555
Stewart, do you respect him?

53
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:03,683
I don't want to murder him,
doesn't mean I like him.

54
00:03:03,684 --> 00:03:05,268
I didn't say like. I said respect.

55
00:03:05,811 --> 00:03:06,812
Well...

56
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:09,898
It's obvious you don't know
anything about Manhunters,

57
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:12,609
so enjoy your solitary fucks.

58
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,987
Is one still alive? On Earth?

59
00:03:22,786 --> 00:03:23,953
What do you know?

60
00:03:23,954 --> 00:03:26,331
Manhunters are believed to be extinct.

61
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,833
I know other things about them too.

62
00:03:28,834 --> 00:03:31,293
Unique aspects of their physiology

63
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:34,089
that cannot be changed
when they take a new form.

64
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,758
If one were alive on your planet,

65
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:41,054
that information would be
of great interest to the Guardians.

66
00:03:43,974 --> 00:03:46,142
Deliver the Manhunter to the Guardians

67
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:47,978
and disgrace Stewart in the process.

68
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:51,856
Tell me, does he speak
to the Guardians directly?

69
00:03:51,857 --> 00:03:53,816
- He says he doesn't.
- And you believed him?

70
00:03:53,817 --> 00:03:56,902
He found out about the Manhunter,
he could've kept it to himself.

71
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,279
All he does is follow orders.

72
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,905
Well, then he can be controlled.

73
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:02,575
Make him believe
that you're embracing his worthiness

74
00:04:02,576 --> 00:04:04,161
as your replacement.

75
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:07,580
- Is he fearless?
- He may be.

76
00:04:07,581 --> 00:04:10,291
Then he will be arrogant,
overly confident,

77
00:04:10,292 --> 00:04:13,003
thus blindly oblivious
to your true intent.

78
00:04:17,215 --> 00:04:19,049
Is that how you fooled me?

79
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:21,011
I was never anything but myself.

80
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,597
My ambition was always a threat.

81
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:26,600
You simply chose not to see it.

82
00:04:29,561 --> 00:04:31,938
Do not make the same mistake
with John Stewart.

83
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:05,263
God damn.

84
00:05:06,515 --> 00:05:08,891
It's that big, green asshole's sidekick.

85
00:05:08,892 --> 00:05:11,269
Hey. Uh, I need a scope.

86
00:05:11,895 --> 00:05:14,021
A Schmidt & Bender,
but I'll take a Leupold

87
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:16,817
or whatever scope
y'all sell with the McMillan.

88
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:19,151
Can't sell you a scope without a gun.

89
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:20,361
Oh, no, I don't want the gun.

90
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:22,279
Well, then you're shit out of luck.

91
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:23,448
It's a package deal.

92
00:05:24,074 --> 00:05:25,617
Kind of like you and your boss.

93
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:27,452
Where is he, anyway?

94
00:05:28,745 --> 00:05:31,956
Okay, I'll, uh, I'll get a rifle
and a scope, please.

95
00:05:31,957 --> 00:05:33,166
Thank you.

96
00:05:42,342 --> 00:05:43,926
Let me guess, if I want the tomato,

97
00:05:43,927 --> 00:05:45,387
I gotta get the ham too?

98
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:56,731
All right, thank you.

99
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,233
Hey.

100
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:00,151
Y'all were a blast.

101
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:23,425
Oh, come on, man.

102
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:27,177
Any sign of our mysterious benefactor?

103
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:28,888
You can just call him a Manhunter.

104
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:30,181
It sounds less stupid.

105
00:06:30,849 --> 00:06:32,433
You think he's coming in on that chopper.

106
00:06:32,434 --> 00:06:33,642
That's why you're up here.

107
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:35,394
See if he lands on that ranch, huh?

108
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:37,021
Couldn't see who's on board.

109
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:38,898
Would've been nice
if you were here since you can fly.

110
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:40,024
Knocked on your door,

111
00:06:40,025 --> 00:06:41,860
- you weren't there.
- I was getting laid in space.

112
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:44,613
Were you worried about me, Junior?

113
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,907
I was concerned about the alien hit squad

114
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:50,452
that's gonna find us
in 36 hours if we don't deliver.

115
00:06:51,036 --> 00:06:52,328
So what'd you learn up here, anyway?

116
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:54,204
The four guard towers on the ranch

117
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:56,332
- share the same line of sight.
- Which means what?

118
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:58,375
Well, I think it means
that there's a hidden structure

119
00:06:58,376 --> 00:06:59,460
on the compound.

120
00:06:59,461 --> 00:07:01,629
One that is obscured
from every vantage point,

121
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:03,422
except those guard towers,

122
00:07:03,423 --> 00:07:05,633
and that's exactly where
that chopper just landed.

123
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:07,093
That building is a weenie.

124
00:07:07,719 --> 00:07:09,595
- What'd you say?
- It's a...

125
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:11,931
It's an architectural term
that Walt Disney made up

126
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:13,599
for structures on his property.

127
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,809
Think Sleeping Beauty's castle
at Disneyland.

128
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:16,895
Wait, wait, wait.

129
00:07:18,188 --> 00:07:19,980
- You've been to Disneyland?
- No, of course not.

130
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,440
They didn't let me in.

131
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:22,983
It's the happiest place on Earth,

132
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:25,236
but they... they said I'd kill the vibe.

133
00:07:25,987 --> 00:07:27,364
Did you just make a joke?

134
00:07:28,782 --> 00:07:30,825
Look, so Walt Disney

135
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:33,994
built his parks around the weenie,

136
00:07:33,995 --> 00:07:36,413
and I'm thinking
that Macon's done the same thing

137
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:38,165
- on his compound.
- So you think the Manhunter's

138
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,667
- inside Macon's weenie?
- Maybe.

139
00:07:39,668 --> 00:07:41,210
I mean, the chopper's easy to track.

140
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:43,796
It lands the same time every day at 9:17.

141
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:47,216
No pilot would do that every day
unless it was on purpose.

142
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:48,842
It could be a decoy.

143
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:52,137
If it is a decoy, then maybe
the Manhunter's not even on the compound.

144
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:53,847
Just gotta get inside to find out.

145
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:55,474
First, we gotta find Sheriff Kane.

146
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:57,643
I gave her my word
that we'd keep her looped in.

147
00:07:57,644 --> 00:07:59,895
Sheriff Kane? Mm-hmm.

148
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:01,481
Mm-hmm, what?

149
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:03,649
She's married.

150
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:07,194
And unlike you,
I respect the matrimonial bond.

151
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,196
I believe you.

152
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,199
Let's go. I'll fly us over.

153
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,243
How's that gonna work?

154
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:16,912
Well, I can either carry you like a baby,

155
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:19,081
or you can hop on
and pretend like I'm a horse.

156
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:20,083
Nah, I'm good.

157
00:08:32,137 --> 00:08:34,096
So, this is your jurisdiction too, huh?

158
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:36,182
My husband owns the bar, so yeah.

159
00:08:36,766 --> 00:08:38,100
Thought he was a lawyer.

160
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:40,311
Everybody in Rushville multi-tasks.

161
00:08:43,982 --> 00:08:44,983
Okay.

162
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,818
Why don't you go with this one?

163
00:08:47,819 --> 00:08:49,570
Really? How much you want me to say?

164
00:08:49,571 --> 00:08:51,613
- Tell her all of it.
- Okay.

165
00:08:51,614 --> 00:08:54,283
Um, so there's
an interplanetary war criminal

166
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:55,784
hiding here in Rushville.

167
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,537
The technical term is a Manhunter.

168
00:08:58,329 --> 00:08:59,330
Sorry.

169
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:01,416
Manhunter?

170
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:03,375
Really?

171
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:05,294
You remember those--
our buddies at the game.

172
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:07,755
Well, the one at the station,
he wasn't the last one.

173
00:09:07,756 --> 00:09:10,091
Apparently there's a crew
of 'em here to assassinate the...

174
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:12,926
well, the thing that John just mentioned.

175
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:13,928
Show her the phone.

176
00:09:15,346 --> 00:09:17,182
So one of them gave me this.

177
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:20,350
They said to call if we find the target.

178
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:22,561
If we don't find it by tomorrow night,

179
00:09:22,562 --> 00:09:24,146
these aliens are going to waltz into town

180
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:25,607
and they're gonna blow up.

181
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:30,110
So what does this thing want?

182
00:09:30,111 --> 00:09:32,529
We don't know, but it's been here a while.

183
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:34,907
How is that possible?
Well, they can take any form.

184
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:37,076
It could be anyone
hiding here in Rushville.

185
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:39,745
So, line everyone up,
put them through those alien detectors.

186
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:40,913
Well, we can't do that.

187
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:43,458
Manhunters aren't alien.
They're something else.

188
00:09:45,210 --> 00:09:46,211
Great.

189
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:50,298
So everybody's a threat
and we're all in danger?

190
00:09:52,383 --> 00:09:54,427
If it could be anyone, why not me?

191
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:56,720
A long time ago,

192
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:58,847
a Lantern by the name
of Abin Sur crashed here.

193
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:01,558
We don't know why,
but there was a Manhunter on board.

194
00:10:01,559 --> 00:10:03,352
Whatever identity that Manhunter took,

195
00:10:03,353 --> 00:10:06,397
well, it wouldn't be
on the records before that.

196
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:10,944
I... I looked you up.
You are from Gotham and...

197
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:15,406
it's a very nice senior photo.
I get why you dropped the bangs.

198
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:19,202
So who's this Manhunter?

199
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:21,996
I'm sure you have a theory.

200
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:24,666
We think it's Macon's benefactor.

201
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:28,252
And because your husband
is Macon's lawyer,

202
00:10:28,253 --> 00:10:29,462
I'm guessing

203
00:10:30,547 --> 00:10:32,715
that you know the moneymaker's identity.

204
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:35,385
Honestly, I don't.

205
00:10:35,969 --> 00:10:37,470
Come on, you're his wife.

206
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:40,556
We don't have that kind of relationship.

207
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:42,141
I've lived here a long time,

208
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:44,018
and I've never seen Macon's money guy.

209
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:47,354
How do you two even think
you're gonna get to him?

210
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:49,231
We think he's in a building on the ranch.

211
00:10:49,232 --> 00:10:51,693
Junior calls it a weenie,
and we're gonna pay a visit to it.

212
00:10:57,157 --> 00:10:59,075
- Okay.
- Okay, that's it?

213
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:02,578
Aliens are gonna blow up my town.

214
00:11:02,579 --> 00:11:04,663
Finding him will stop them, right?

215
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,457
Right. Probably.

216
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,670
You're only gonna get one shot at this.

217
00:11:11,337 --> 00:11:12,463
Do not miss.

218
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:32,399
Hey, you think...

219
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,235
Sheriff's gonna tell Macon we're coming?

220
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:37,196
That would not be good.

221
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:38,989
- But you don't think she will?
- I do not.

222
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:41,033
- And that's your gut?
- My gut, always.

223
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,702
Okay, so now what?

224
00:11:43,286 --> 00:11:44,369
We wait.

225
00:11:44,370 --> 00:11:46,205
- For what?
- Nightfall.

226
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:49,167
Better to burn six hours
than die in broad daylight.

227
00:11:56,591 --> 00:11:57,634
Copy that.

228
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:15,610
You failed to make contact.

229
00:12:17,028 --> 00:12:18,862
This is disappointing.

230
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:19,864
I'm sorry.

231
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,575
Jordan's nearby taking a nap.

232
00:12:23,201 --> 00:12:24,910
I was afraid he'd know if I left.

233
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:26,703
What are you still doing in Nebraska?

234
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:28,248
We're just cleaning up

235
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,875
from the alien that self-destructed.

236
00:12:31,542 --> 00:12:33,877
Did Jordan tell you
where he traveled last evening?

237
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:36,172
He said he was having sex in space.

238
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:39,300
That's a lie.

239
00:12:39,801 --> 00:12:41,301
Okay, where was he?

240
00:12:41,302 --> 00:12:42,804
Violating his oath.

241
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:46,557
He went to see Sinestro.

242
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:49,810
What did they talk about?

243
00:12:49,811 --> 00:12:51,395
I was hoping you could tell me.

244
00:12:51,396 --> 00:12:52,479
He doesn't tell me shit.

245
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:55,232
What's important is that Jordan's actions

246
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:57,026
have accelerated the inevitable.

247
00:12:58,569 --> 00:13:00,363
I've spoken to the other Guardians.

248
00:13:01,614 --> 00:13:02,740
We're in agreement.

249
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:06,285
During the course of your training,

250
00:13:06,286 --> 00:13:08,829
- Jordan gives you the ring, yes?
- Yeah.

251
00:13:08,830 --> 00:13:10,832
The moment you put it on your finger,

252
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:13,042
recite the oath,

253
00:13:14,294 --> 00:13:18,673
and you become
Green Lantern for Sector 2814.

254
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:22,927
And that's it?

255
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:25,512
We agreed you would replace him.

256
00:13:25,513 --> 00:13:26,930
Yeah, I just didn't realize

257
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:29,017
that you were gonna make me do it myself.

258
00:13:30,143 --> 00:13:31,268
I did not realize

259
00:13:31,269 --> 00:13:32,979
that your father's weakness
runs within you.

260
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:37,774
I was promised by your mother
that that was not the case.

261
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,401
Your mother was wrong.

262
00:13:39,402 --> 00:13:41,403
I doubted at first when she told me

263
00:13:41,404 --> 00:13:44,282
that you were strong,
and that you had integrity,

264
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:47,659
and that your makeup was sublime
and above most of the others,

265
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:49,329
that your potential was enormous.

266
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:51,831
I hesitated,

267
00:13:52,457 --> 00:13:54,667
and I should have
trusted my own instincts.

268
00:13:55,585 --> 00:13:58,713
Jordan has filed multiple reports
about your progress.

269
00:14:00,298 --> 00:14:02,299
He says you lack creativity.

270
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:04,052
He says that you are too weak

271
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:07,179
to bear the massive power of the ring.

272
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,140
Well, that's because he's old.

273
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:12,560
And he's tired. And his time is up.

274
00:14:14,020 --> 00:14:16,438
He's not worthy of
the "massive power" of the ring.

275
00:14:16,439 --> 00:14:19,524
He didn't do shit to earn it.
And every time he looks at me,

276
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:22,652
he realizes that I'll do this better
than he's ever done it before

277
00:14:22,653 --> 00:14:25,114
because I've worked
my entire fucking life for it.

278
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:30,036
The ring's always been mine.

279
00:14:31,621 --> 00:14:33,664
That asshole's just keeping it warm.

280
00:14:35,708 --> 00:14:37,168
Then go and get it.

281
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,422
John Stewart.

282
00:14:59,107 --> 00:15:00,524
- You all right?
- Hey, listen.

283
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:02,859
I know you're probably
planning on just flying in

284
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,069
with your big green fist

285
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:05,904
and smashing shit
until you get to the weenie,

286
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:07,948
and I don't want to tell you
how to do your job.

287
00:15:07,949 --> 00:15:09,908
- Well, then don't.
- But each of those guard towers

288
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,827
are going to be manned
with three sharpshooters,

289
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:13,663
and it will be your head next time.

290
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:17,750
So, I suggest
you tunnel in from underground.

291
00:15:18,584 --> 00:15:20,586
Well, how do you propose I do that?

292
00:15:27,093 --> 00:15:28,510
Did you draw this just now?

293
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:29,846
Yeah, I'm creative.

294
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:31,931
Let's go.

295
00:15:47,155 --> 00:15:49,198
Here. You manifest it.

296
00:15:52,785 --> 00:15:53,870
What?

297
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:56,539
We'll call it today's lesson.

298
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:58,374
Go ahead.

299
00:16:24,484 --> 00:16:25,526
Let's dig.

300
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,031
Yeah.

301
00:17:00,061 --> 00:17:01,604
"Five degrees to the left."

302
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:06,399
- How do you know all this?
- Did some research online.

303
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,860
I don't buy it. You're a Marine sniper.

304
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,071
Yeah, and after I was a Marine sniper,

305
00:17:11,072 --> 00:17:12,281
I went to art school.

306
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:17,954
- Who the fuck are you?
- Trying to concentrate.

307
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:19,996
Well, you should be able to concentrate

308
00:17:19,997 --> 00:17:22,040
and take personal questions
at the same time.

309
00:17:22,041 --> 00:17:24,418
- Right.
- How's your mom?

310
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:27,754
She's great. How's your mom?

311
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:28,923
Dead. Cancer.

312
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:31,717
Jesus.

313
00:17:32,218 --> 00:17:34,512
- Both your parents?
- Concentrate, will you?

314
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:37,431
It makes it easier. No ties.

315
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:39,433
Oh, I'm sorry.

316
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:41,852
Don't be sorry.

317
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:45,940
My mom had a good life, and my dad, he...

318
00:17:46,649 --> 00:17:49,025
died the way he wanted to, a hero.

319
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,111
What was he like?

320
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:52,655
Fearless.

321
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:55,741
At least, that's what
he wanted people to think.

322
00:17:56,867 --> 00:17:58,119
What was he afraid of?

323
00:18:07,003 --> 00:18:08,004
We're here.

324
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:57,154
No benefactor, but what the fuck?

325
00:19:58,197 --> 00:20:00,700
These weapons are too high-tech
to be from around here.

326
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:03,369
We were right.

327
00:20:04,120 --> 00:20:06,747
- Benefactor's the Manhunter.
- Yeah.

328
00:20:07,331 --> 00:20:08,457
Give me my ring.

329
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:16,297
I just heard a click.
Did you just hear a click?

330
00:20:16,298 --> 00:20:18,007
Yeah. I just heard a click.

331
00:20:18,008 --> 00:20:19,218
Don't move.

332
00:20:19,719 --> 00:20:22,722
It's a pressure alarm.
If you move, it'll set it off.

333
00:20:23,431 --> 00:20:24,890
- A good movie.
- Great movie.

334
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:28,893
So, we just make it believe
that I'm still standing on it.

335
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:30,938
Yeah, okay. How much do you weigh?

336
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:32,898
One-eighty-five. Ish.

337
00:20:33,399 --> 00:20:34,400
Okay.

338
00:20:47,037 --> 00:20:49,039
Okay, we're gonna
do this at the same time.

339
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:51,709
Three.

340
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,502
Two.

341
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,212
One.

342
00:20:56,422 --> 00:20:57,506
I did say ish.

343
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:23,282
Fuck! I can't see!

344
00:21:23,866 --> 00:21:25,367
Do something, Junior!

345
00:21:26,118 --> 00:21:27,703
For Christ's sake, use the ring!

346
00:21:28,287 --> 00:21:29,663
It's not fucking working!

347
00:21:42,176 --> 00:21:43,677
Yes, sir. Two hundred a head.

348
00:21:45,763 --> 00:21:47,139
Tonight.

349
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:05,616
My wife tells me you're an artist.

350
00:22:07,451 --> 00:22:08,743
Yeah, she's right.

351
00:22:08,744 --> 00:22:10,162
Are you talented?

352
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:14,792
Draw me.

353
00:22:18,963 --> 00:22:20,214
What's your medium?

354
00:22:21,215 --> 00:22:22,216
Charcoal.

355
00:22:23,133 --> 00:22:24,218
Charcoal.

356
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:26,178
Some good stock.

357
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:31,724
Hey, I've seen some shit,

358
00:22:31,725 --> 00:22:34,394
even been to a planet
with sentient tentacles,

359
00:22:34,395 --> 00:22:36,230
- but this is weird, right?
- Yeah.

360
00:23:02,882 --> 00:23:04,633
You better get to doodling, Junior.

361
00:23:07,136 --> 00:23:08,262
Hit me.

362
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:12,266
Take a seat. Relax your hands.

363
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:19,356
Hold it there. Thank you.

364
00:23:23,444 --> 00:23:25,029
Zoe, honey, why don't you stay?

365
00:23:29,158 --> 00:23:30,159
Okay.

366
00:23:34,622 --> 00:23:36,164
You can holster up, partner.

367
00:23:36,165 --> 00:23:38,333
Junior here, he can draw from memory.

368
00:23:38,334 --> 00:23:39,792
Is that right?

369
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,545
Well, then you could probably
draw my wife.

370
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:47,842
Can we talk
about the elephant in the room?

371
00:23:47,843 --> 00:23:49,803
- Which elephant?
- Not that one.

372
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:51,930
What goes on in this ranch?

373
00:23:51,931 --> 00:23:53,473
Your guys, they shot darkness at us.

374
00:23:53,474 --> 00:23:54,557
Now, call me paranoid,

375
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:57,186
but those guns seem tailor-made
for disabling Green Lanterns.

376
00:23:57,811 --> 00:24:00,063
Hey, I told you.
We're ready for any kind of invasion.

377
00:24:00,064 --> 00:24:02,023
Well, that's kind of worrisome, isn't it?

378
00:24:02,024 --> 00:24:05,069
Well, it should only be worrisome
if the Lanterns pose a threat to my boss.

379
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:07,446
So now he's your boss?

380
00:24:08,030 --> 00:24:09,739
I thought he was just the benefactor.

381
00:24:09,740 --> 00:24:11,240
Don't get caught up in semantics.

382
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:12,325
Boss, benefactor...

383
00:24:12,326 --> 00:24:14,161
- How about savior?
- Sure.

384
00:24:14,828 --> 00:24:16,121
He did cure my cancer.

385
00:24:18,457 --> 00:24:20,542
That's how we met. Zoe was my nurse.

386
00:24:21,377 --> 00:24:23,712
Kept me alive
after the doctor said I was a goner.

387
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:27,174
Then he came,
worked his magic, and voilà.

388
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:31,011
- "His magic"?
- So to speak.

389
00:24:32,096 --> 00:24:34,973
- Can you relax your shoulders?
- Now you talk about him like he's a god.

390
00:24:34,974 --> 00:24:36,725
- I do, don't I?
- Hey, please.

391
00:24:37,226 --> 00:24:38,560
Could you just stay still?

392
00:24:42,189 --> 00:24:44,066
Everything changed when he showed up.

393
00:24:45,442 --> 00:24:49,445
Crops grow. Kids thrive.
And you saw the hospital.

394
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:50,781
No one gets sick.

395
