He takes care of us
in exchange for our protection.

396
00:24:56,662 --> 00:24:59,373
So why don't you leave
so we can protect him?

397
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:02,459
Well, that's not gonna happen.

398
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:07,256
Well, that's unfortunate.

399
00:25:11,010 --> 00:25:13,594
How about we skip the bluff
where you threaten to kill me

400
00:25:13,595 --> 00:25:15,014
with a darkness gun?

401
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:18,433
'Cause we both know if I end up dead,

402
00:25:18,434 --> 00:25:20,601
there's gonna be 100 Lanterns
at your front door,

403
00:25:20,602 --> 00:25:22,812
and you're not even gonna
have time to hide my body.

404
00:25:22,813 --> 00:25:23,896
You're right.

405
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:27,192
Killing a Lantern
would trigger a large response.

406
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:31,613
He's not a Lantern.

407
00:25:33,782 --> 00:25:36,492
Dad, please put your dick away.

408
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:39,912
- Can I help you, Sheriff?
- I got a call about trespassers.

409
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:42,749
- Gonna assume it was these two.
- You're making a mistake, Kerry.

410
00:25:42,750 --> 00:25:44,333
Just turn around and leave us be.

411
00:25:44,334 --> 00:25:47,128
- That's not gonna happen.
- That's exactly what I said.

412
00:25:47,129 --> 00:25:49,048
Let's go. I'm taking you in.

413
00:25:50,549 --> 00:25:51,592
Move.

414
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:18,577
You had one shot
to get the guy and you whiffed.

415
00:26:19,078 --> 00:26:22,121
If Zoe hadn't called me,
you'd be beyond fucked.

416
00:26:22,122 --> 00:26:23,414
I live in beyond fucked.

417
00:26:23,415 --> 00:26:25,333
Jesus, what is that, a catchphrase?

418
00:26:25,334 --> 00:26:29,838
Do you hear yourself?
I'm in this shit with you now.

419
00:26:36,386 --> 00:26:37,804
I broke into Billy's files.

420
00:26:37,805 --> 00:26:40,724
I am this close
to finding your stupid benefactor.

421
00:26:41,266 --> 00:26:43,852
Until I do, you're gonna lock your doors

422
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:47,396
and you're gonna wait
for me to tell you what happens next.

423
00:26:47,397 --> 00:26:48,565
Is that clear?

424
00:26:51,401 --> 00:26:52,986
Yes. Yes.

425
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:56,531
Superheroes don't really
lock their doors--

426
00:26:56,532 --> 00:26:57,533
- Say yes!
- Yes.

427
00:26:58,534 --> 00:26:59,535
Good.

428
00:27:00,244 --> 00:27:01,495
You're free to go.

429
00:27:04,498 --> 00:27:05,832
You kinda gotta let us out.

430
00:27:05,833 --> 00:27:06,917
Oh my God.

431
00:27:16,927 --> 00:27:17,928
Wait.

432
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:23,183
Sheriff, not even a date first?

433
00:27:23,684 --> 00:27:24,977
Do you ever shut up?

434
00:27:25,686 --> 00:27:27,229
Stewart, come here.

435
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:31,315
Macon let you just walk off his ranch.

436
00:27:31,316 --> 00:27:33,109
He's not done with you two yet.

437
00:27:33,110 --> 00:27:35,612
He knows where you are.
He'll send someone.

438
00:27:37,573 --> 00:27:39,448
I'd take you into protective custody,

439
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:42,118
but we're still trying
to put the station back together, so...

440
00:27:42,119 --> 00:27:43,287
Yeah, thank you.

441
00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:45,581
Nothing for me?

442
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:48,750
You're a superhero.

443
00:28:04,057 --> 00:28:05,100
Hey, Junior.

444
00:28:07,895 --> 00:28:08,896
What?

445
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:11,982
We found Macon's weenie.

446
00:28:18,614 --> 00:28:20,489
<i>Why are you calling me on your cell?</i>

447
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:21,741
<i>Get to the payphone.</i>

448
00:28:21,742 --> 00:28:23,327
I talked to them already, Mama.

449
00:28:24,203 --> 00:28:25,287
<i>What did they say?</i>

450
00:28:27,748 --> 00:28:29,291
They're not gonna give me the ring.

451
00:28:30,083 --> 00:28:31,500
They're making me take it from him.

452
00:28:31,501 --> 00:28:32,835
<i>Then take it.</i>

453
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:34,629
<i>Don't tell me you fell for that man.</i>

454
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:35,755
Oh, come on.

455
00:28:35,756 --> 00:28:37,423
<i>He is a charming motherfucker.</i>

456
00:28:37,424 --> 00:28:39,133
I know exactly what the fuck he is.

457
00:28:39,134 --> 00:28:41,220
<i>Good. Don't lose focus.</i>

458
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:43,555
I won't.

459
00:28:48,143 --> 00:28:49,311
Mama, I gotta go.

460
00:29:14,044 --> 00:29:15,587
Want to put that thing away?

461
00:29:18,340 --> 00:29:19,549
What are you doing here?

462
00:29:21,009 --> 00:29:22,386
Did Macon send you?

463
00:29:23,553 --> 00:29:25,347
No. I came on my own.

464
00:29:27,057 --> 00:29:28,892
Then why are you here?

465
00:30:31,163 --> 00:30:35,042
I was thinking
how much better that is not in my truck.

466
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:51,433
This has to be the last time.

467
00:30:54,895 --> 00:30:55,896
Okay.

468
00:30:57,522 --> 00:30:58,899
Is there a reason why?

469
00:31:01,151 --> 00:31:04,029
Well, your choices
are pretty much leave town or get killed.

470
00:31:05,906 --> 00:31:08,033
I really hope you choose the former.

471
00:31:12,829 --> 00:31:13,830
I'm sorry.

472
00:31:16,750 --> 00:31:18,043
Why are you staying?

473
00:31:21,129 --> 00:31:25,217
Because I feel
like everybody's lying to me.

474
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:28,804
Why?

475
00:31:31,723 --> 00:31:33,642
Because that's exactly what I'm doing.

476
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:38,480
You think Jordan is lying to you?

477
00:31:38,980 --> 00:31:39,981
Yeah.

478
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:43,485
Do you think I am?

479
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:48,532
Yeah.

480
00:31:58,250 --> 00:32:01,044
When I tell you what I know...

481
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:04,339
everything changes.

482
00:32:07,926 --> 00:32:09,052
I can't do that.

483
00:32:09,970 --> 00:32:11,388
Because of your husband?

484
00:32:13,890 --> 00:32:15,183
What do you owe him?

485
00:32:15,684 --> 00:32:18,145
You read this all wrong. I don't owe him.

486
00:32:19,855 --> 00:32:21,022
He owes me.

487
00:32:22,149 --> 00:32:24,860
He was dying
when I met him and I saved his life.

488
00:32:25,527 --> 00:32:26,570
And now...

489
00:32:27,404 --> 00:32:30,031
I am trying to save yours.

490
00:32:36,079 --> 00:32:37,289
Is that a yes?

491
00:32:38,540 --> 00:32:39,624
You'll leave town?

492
00:32:43,211 --> 00:32:44,337
Not a chance.

493
00:32:47,299 --> 00:32:48,425
<i>Damn.</i>

494
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:51,636
Damn.

495
00:33:43,605 --> 00:33:45,105
Where'd it come from?

496
00:33:45,106 --> 00:33:47,192
- Forty-five degrees northeast.
- Just fucking point!

497
00:34:32,445 --> 00:34:34,280
Who the hell makes a satellite like this?

498
00:34:34,281 --> 00:34:39,244
I've narrowed it down to Atlas,
Vermond, and Rutger.

499
00:34:41,162 --> 00:34:43,790
Macon signed NDAs
with all three companies.

500
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:45,457
When?

501
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:47,294
All three were over ten years ago.

502
00:34:47,877 --> 00:34:51,338
Atlas and Rutger, around 30.

503
00:34:51,339 --> 00:34:53,591
It's gotta be one of them then.
Junior, you almost done?

504
00:34:53,592 --> 00:34:55,051
Yeah, good. Almost done.

505
00:34:56,219 --> 00:34:57,846
She was his grandmother.

506
00:34:58,388 --> 00:35:00,223
What am I supposed to tell Noah?

507
00:35:07,814 --> 00:35:09,774
Just tell him we're gonna
find out whoever did this.

508
00:35:11,735 --> 00:35:13,777
Every satellite's registered
with the government.

509
00:35:13,778 --> 00:35:14,779
Can you run that?

510
00:35:15,322 --> 00:35:18,575
I can run the serial number
through the FCC database.

511
00:35:24,706 --> 00:35:26,958
It's registered to Atlas, Inc.

512
00:35:27,626 --> 00:35:30,210
Owner of Atlas, Inc. is Hector Hammond.

513
00:35:30,211 --> 00:35:33,547
Runs a string of high-tech slaughterhouses
across the country.

514
00:35:33,548 --> 00:35:37,302
No record of him anywhere before 1986.

515
00:35:37,927 --> 00:35:39,596
Where's his nearest slaughterhouse?

516
00:35:40,722 --> 00:35:42,056
Ninety-five miles away.

517
00:35:42,057 --> 00:35:44,141
That's where he's gonna be then.
I'd bet Junior's life on it.

518
00:35:44,142 --> 00:35:46,353
- What do you say?
- I think it seems too easy.

519
00:35:48,188 --> 00:35:49,271
Elaborate.

520
00:35:49,272 --> 00:35:51,148
You're the space cop.
Where's the investigation?

521
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:53,652
You think we just cracked
the case in this motel room?

522
00:35:55,904 --> 00:35:56,987
Go on.

523
00:35:56,988 --> 00:35:59,991
Well, he's got all these satellites
that can kill us all at any time.

524
00:36:01,201 --> 00:36:02,452
But we're still alive.

525
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:05,121
And why did he choose
to kill Zoe and not us?

526
00:36:07,582 --> 00:36:09,709
Because killing Zoe
was more than just a threat.

527
00:36:10,335 --> 00:36:11,752
It was an invitation.

528
00:36:11,753 --> 00:36:15,215
Jesus, Junior. That's not bad. Nice work.

529
00:36:16,549 --> 00:36:17,550
Thanks.

530
00:36:22,389 --> 00:36:24,140
Hey, Earth to Stewart.

531
00:36:27,477 --> 00:36:28,603
<i>Earth to Stewart.</i>

532
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:32,232
How you doing?

533
00:36:35,819 --> 00:36:36,902
What?

534
00:36:36,903 --> 00:36:39,030
You have never asked me that before.

535
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:43,201
Your girlfriend blew up in front of you.

536
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:46,079
I'm handling it.

537
00:36:49,207 --> 00:36:51,292
Kinda look like
you're shutting down your feelings.

538
00:36:56,297 --> 00:36:57,507
It's part of the job.

539
00:36:58,341 --> 00:37:00,135
People dying is part of the job.

540
00:37:02,887 --> 00:37:04,097
You want some advice?

541
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:09,018
Avoid real relationships from here on out.

542
00:37:09,519 --> 00:37:12,439
Keep people at a distance
for their own safety.

543
00:37:16,359 --> 00:37:18,486
It's a lonely fucking job.

544
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:25,076
You ever talk with the other Lanterns?

545
00:37:26,703 --> 00:37:28,746
I'm the only human. They're aliens.

546
00:37:28,747 --> 00:37:30,080
One of them's a fucking squirrel.

547
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:32,667
- Nobody like me.
- I'm like you. I'm human.

548
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:36,044
That you are.

549
00:37:36,045 --> 00:37:38,130
Yet you hate having me as a backup.

550
00:37:38,131 --> 00:37:39,132
I do.

551
00:37:40,341 --> 00:37:41,509
What's the plan?

552
00:37:44,179 --> 00:37:45,180
I say...

553
00:37:46,681 --> 00:37:48,349
we walk straight into his trap.

554
00:37:50,518 --> 00:37:51,853
You wanna hear my idea?

555
00:37:52,854 --> 00:37:54,272
I say you give me the ring.

556
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:56,774
Okay, Hammond's gonna
expect you to have it,

557
00:37:56,775 --> 00:37:58,109
not me, element of surprise.

558
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:00,694
- So I'm a decoy.
- Yeah, you would be.

559
00:38:00,695 --> 00:38:03,363
Oh, this isn't a training exercise.
You're good, but you're no me.

560
00:38:03,364 --> 00:38:04,532
Maybe next time.

561
00:38:05,033 --> 00:38:06,034
Hey.

562
00:38:06,576 --> 00:38:07,911
I like the confidence, though.

563
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:20,297
<i>Remember, security.</i>

564
00:38:20,298 --> 00:38:22,759
<i>The first step towards
a safer environment.</i>

565
00:38:23,343 --> 00:38:25,720
<i>Stay secure, stay vigilant.</i>

566
00:38:28,890 --> 00:38:30,099
<i>Remember, security.</i>

567
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:32,977
<i>The first step
towards a safer environment.</i>

568
00:38:33,937 --> 00:38:35,897
<i>Stay secure, stay vigilant.</i>

569
00:39:01,798 --> 00:39:03,925
Hey, where's Hammond?

570
00:39:23,862 --> 00:39:25,571
I'm about done
with these weird-ass people.

571
00:39:25,572 --> 00:39:26,573
Agreed.

572
00:39:45,425 --> 00:39:48,428
Jazz, that can't be good.

573
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:07,822
Well, we found the cows.

574
00:40:46,736 --> 00:40:47,862
That's why I'm vegan.

575
00:41:08,633 --> 00:41:10,175
Mr. Hammond, I assume.

576
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:12,010
3248 Aspen Way.

577
00:41:12,011 --> 00:41:14,639
- How's that?
- That's my parents' address.

578
00:41:15,431 --> 00:41:17,684
I've already shown you
what my satellites are capable of.

579
00:41:18,601 --> 00:41:20,645
In exactly three minutes

580
00:41:21,562 --> 00:41:23,981
one of them
will obliterate your childhood home,

581
00:41:23,982 --> 00:41:26,733
unless I enter a code onto this laptop.

582
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:28,694
You kill me, you kill them.

583
00:41:28,695 --> 00:41:29,820
Yeah, that's great.

584
00:41:29,821 --> 00:41:32,197
Dead man's trigger.
Don't act like you invented it.

585
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:34,408
Look, you invited us here.
Let's get down to business, huh?

586
00:41:34,409 --> 00:41:37,327
You can save them, John.
Would you like to know how?

587
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:39,037
Don't talk to him. You talk to me.

588
00:41:39,038 --> 00:41:40,831
You were approached
by a group of individuals

589
00:41:40,832 --> 00:41:42,165
searching for me.

590
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:44,209
They gave you a phone. Call them.

591
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:45,670
Tell them you found me right here.

592
00:41:46,462 --> 00:41:49,381
All right, so you can use
the old, uh, cow laser on them.

593
00:41:49,382 --> 00:41:51,049
All right, that... that's clever.

594
00:41:51,050 --> 00:41:52,467
Quick question.

595
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:53,844
How do you know about John's phone?

596
00:41:53,845 --> 00:41:58,015
Is he always like this?
It must be insufferable.

597
00:41:58,016 --> 00:42:00,017
You're gonna suffer
if you don't start talking to me.

598
00:42:00,018 --> 00:42:01,936
- I'm the one with the ring.
- For now.

599
00:42:02,562 --> 00:42:03,645
What does that mean?

600
00:42:03,646 --> 00:42:06,816
When you checked into the motel,
I decided it best to listen in.

601
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:09,401
I've been monitoring
your conversations there.

602
00:42:09,402 --> 00:42:10,945
Most of them were boring.

603
00:42:12,822 --> 00:42:13,823
Most.

604
00:42:16,659 --> 00:42:18,744
<i>That's because he's old.</i>

605
00:42:18,745 --> 00:42:21,539
<i>And he's tired. And his time is up.</i>

606
00:42:23,041 --> 00:42:25,333
<i>He's not worthy
of the "massive power" of the ring.</i>

607
00:42:25,334 --> 00:42:28,128
<i>He didn't do shit to earn it.
And every time he looks at me,</i>

608
00:42:28,129 --> 00:42:31,590
<i>he realizes that I'll do this better
than he's ever done it before</i>

609
00:42:31,591 --> 00:42:33,968
<i>because I've worked
my entire fucking life for it.</i>

610
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:38,931
<i>The ring's always been mine.</i>

611
00:42:40,600 --> 00:42:42,351
<i>That asshole's just keeping it warm.</i>

612
00:42:43,019 --> 00:42:44,353
<i>Then go and get it.</i>

613
00:42:46,064 --> 00:42:47,565
You're obsolete, Mr. Jordan.

614
00:42:48,107 --> 00:42:51,610
Replaced by a new
and vastly improved model.

615
00:42:51,611 --> 00:42:53,654
That must be terrifying.

616
00:42:55,031 --> 00:42:57,491
- What color is Abin Sur?
- What?

617
00:42:57,492 --> 00:42:58,992
The fellow who gave me this ring,

618
00:42:58,993 --> 00:43:01,661
who dropped you off
on this planet before he died?

619
00:43:01,662 --> 00:43:03,664
You're the Manhunter. What color was he?

620
00:43:05,875 --> 00:43:08,376
- I don't remember.
- He was a very memorable shade.

621
00:43:08,377 --> 00:43:09,878
I've met a lot of aliens.

622
00:43:09,879 --> 00:43:11,172
I don't think you have.

623
00:43:12,381 --> 00:43:13,799
I think you're bullshit.

624
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:16,594
I think you're a smokescreen
for someone else. A decoy.

625
00:43:17,512 --> 00:43:18,721
One minute and counting.

626
00:43:19,388 --> 00:43:20,764
You know, an old friend of mine

627
00:43:20,765 --> 00:43:22,849
recently told me
something about Manhunters.

628
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:24,726
Very good at replicating other organisms,

629
00:43:24,727 --> 00:43:25,770
nearly perfect.

630
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:29,065
But when it comes
to copying carbon-based life forms,

631
00:43:29,857 --> 00:43:32,443
the only organ
you can't get just right is the heart.

632
00:43:33,069 --> 00:43:36,489
It's an undetectable flaw,
when you're alive.

633
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:40,660
But once your heart stops,
it crystallizes.

634
00:43:41,661 --> 00:43:43,830
So the only way
to prove that you're a Manhunter

635
00:43:44,664 --> 00:43:46,540
is to rip your fucking heart out.

636
00:43:46,541 --> 00:43:48,250
You kill me, his parents die.

637
00:43:48,251 --> 00:43:49,835
I got no problem with that.

638
00:43:49,836 --> 00:43:52,379
I mean, I would have given
a shit before the recording,

639
00:43:52,380 --> 00:43:54,005
but now I'm starting to think, you know,

640
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:57,467
a hero's journey, it should really
only start after the parents are dead.

641
00:43:57,468 --> 00:43:59,719
- The fuck are you doing?
- You kill Stewart's family,

642
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:01,472
I got no reason to keep you alive.

643
00:44:02,765 --> 00:44:05,143
So you got
about ten seconds to tell me the truth.

644
00:44:05,935 --> 00:44:07,228
- Hal.
- Nine.

645
00:44:07,812 --> 00:44:09,104
- Eight.
- Stop.

646
00:44:09,105 --> 00:44:10,730
- Seven.
- Stop!

647
00:44:10,731 --> 00:44:11,940
- Six.
- Stop!

648
00:44:11,941 --> 00:44:13,192
I'm human! I'm human!

649
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:15,778
Fucking put in that code right now.

650
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:25,830
- They're safe.
- What if you were fucking wrong?

651
00:44:26,914 --> 00:44:28,040
I'm never wrong.

652
00:44:29,834 --> 00:44:30,918
Okay.

653
00:44:32,044 --> 00:44:33,254
Okay, who are you?

654
00:44:34,505 --> 00:44:38,050
- Who the fuck are you? Speak up!
- I'm Hector Gutierrez.

655
00:44:39,635 --> 00:44:41,219
I was an engineering student.

656
00:44:41,220 --> 00:44:44,014
He came to me,
offering me incredible technology,

657
00:44:44,015 --> 00:44:45,599
said I could use it to help my family,

658
00:44:45,600 --> 00:44:47,977
- my community.
- Who the fuck is the Manhunter?

659
00:44:49,854 --> 00:44:51,063
Isn't it obvious?

660
00:44:54,275 --> 00:44:55,860
Will Macon.

661
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:23,179
I was gonna give it back.

662
00:45:24,388 --> 00:45:25,389
What?

663
00:45:29,101 --> 00:45:32,647
At Macon's ranch, I was wearing the ring.

664
00:45:35,024 --> 00:45:37,109
All I needed to do was say the oath.

665
00:45:38,402 --> 00:45:39,612
But I didn't.

666
00:45:41,781 --> 00:45:43,366
And when I asked for it again,

667
00:45:43,908 --> 00:45:46,118
I just wanted to show you
what I was capable of.

668
00:45:49,038 --> 00:45:50,039
I believe you.

669
00:45:50,998 --> 00:45:52,875
- It's all good.
- Really?

670
00:45:54,669 --> 00:45:56,504
Honestly, I'd have done the same thing.

671
00:45:57,213 --> 00:45:59,422
And what you said wasn't all untrue.

672
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:01,091
I didn't do much to earn this thing.

673
00:46:01,092 --> 00:46:04,470
And there's a very good chance
that you might end up being better.

674
00:46:07,515 --> 00:46:10,142
I can be a bit of an asshole at times.

675
00:46:15,189 --> 00:46:17,400
You know, the Guardian
said you broke a vow.

676
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:21,237
You believe everything they say.

677
00:46:22,280 --> 00:46:23,990
You ought to give that a rest.

678
00:46:24,532 --> 00:46:26,575
I mean, look what they're doing to me now.

679
00:46:27,201 --> 00:46:29,161
But that said, I did break a vow.

680
00:46:30,913 --> 00:46:32,540
Went to see Sinestro.

681
00:46:33,874 --> 00:46:35,668
So he told you about the crystal heart?

682
00:46:36,168 --> 00:46:37,669
Among other things.

683
00:46:37,670 --> 00:46:39,046
They're ruthless, Junior.

684
00:46:39,714 --> 00:46:42,632
They assimilate into communities
by attaching to weak spots.

685
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:44,010
It's what they're programmed to do.

686
00:46:44,677 --> 00:46:47,012
So what you're saying
is they have no other choice?

687
00:46:47,013 --> 00:46:48,555
They find a path to power every time,

688
00:46:48,556 --> 00:46:50,683
and if they identify
a threat to that power,

689
00:46:51,183 --> 00:46:52,475
they'll manipulate that threat

690
00:46:52,476 --> 00:46:54,270
into believing anything they want them to.

691
00:46:55,980 --> 00:46:57,440
Remind you of anyone we know?

692
00:47:08,492 --> 00:47:09,660
Yeah, it must be Macon.

693
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:12,663
Like Hector said.

694
00:47:16,542 --> 00:47:17,543
Yeah.

695
00:47:32,183 --> 00:47:33,934
Call that alien hit squad.

696
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:37,854
Tell them to meet us at the cafe.

697
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:39,190
Nah, they don't trust you.

698
00:47:41,192 --> 00:47:43,569
Why don't you tell them
to meet you at the cafe, then?

699
00:47:45,196 --> 00:47:46,238
They trust you.

700
00:47:55,164 --> 00:47:56,207
Yeah.

701
00:48:04,840 --> 00:48:07,885
<i>- Yeah?</i>
- I've got who we're looking for.

702
00:48:09,512 --> 00:48:10,595
<i>That's good.</i>

703
00:48:10,596 --> 00:48:14,392
Meet me at the cafe
just outside of Rushville.

704
00:48:16,602 --> 00:48:17,728
<i>We're close.</i>

705
00:48:20,481 --> 00:48:21,482
Yeah.

706
00:48:29,824 --> 00:48:30,825
What?

707
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:34,120
I really did forgive you.

708
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:38,582
Thought you'd be honest.

709
00:48:43,712 --> 00:48:44,713
About what?

710
00:48:45,256 --> 00:48:48,174
When Zoe blew up,
I didn't get why you weren't upset.

711
00:48:48,175 --> 00:48:50,010
I thought you were made of stone.

712
00:48:51,720 --> 00:48:53,639
I wondered why you weren't sad.

713
00:48:55,141 --> 00:48:56,475
I knew you liked her.

714
00:48:58,644 --> 00:48:59,854
Now, with Hector,

715
00:49:00,729 --> 00:49:02,815
when you freaked out
about your parents, and...

716
00:49:03,482 --> 00:49:04,733
it kinda all hit me.

717
00:49:06,277 --> 00:49:07,903
You ain't made of stone, Junior.

718
00:49:09,405 --> 00:49:12,157
You aren't upset
because you know Zoe isn't dead.

719
00:49:12,158 --> 00:49:13,491
And I don't know how she managed

720
00:49:13,492 --> 00:49:15,660
to get out of that car alive
unless she's a Manhunter.

721
00:49:15,661 --> 00:49:17,329
The thing that I can't figure out

722
00:49:17,872 --> 00:49:19,123
is how long you've known.

723
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:22,334
I didn't know. I just had a feeling.

724
00:49:22,835 --> 00:49:24,961
Fuck feeling, that's your gut, Junior.

725
00:49:24,962 --> 00:49:26,838
- Yeah.
- Well, bravo.

726
00:49:26,839 --> 00:49:28,590
Congratulations, truly.

727
00:49:28,591 --> 00:49:31,050
The student surpasses the teacher.

728
00:49:31,051 --> 00:49:33,261
I wasn't trying to keep anything from you.

729
00:49:33,262 --> 00:49:35,889
I just didn't know for certain,
so I didn't want to say anything.

730
00:49:35,890 --> 00:49:37,307
Oh, you haven't told the Guardians?

731
00:49:37,308 --> 00:49:39,517
I haven't told the Guardians
anything we've been doing

732
00:49:39,518 --> 00:49:40,977
because you asked me not to.

733
00:49:40,978 --> 00:49:42,938
- Right?
- Except that I'm old and tired.

734
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:47,610
Well, I'm sorry about that.

735
00:49:48,986 --> 00:49:50,362
I'm sorry about the rental.

